      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This article presents many products used against asthma since half of 19th century, until they've been took off from the market, in 1992. Thoses products were used in fumigation or inhalation, without any complex machine. They were powders, impragnated papers, cigares an cigarets. They contained more often nitrates and Solanacées. An exemple of struggle between two specialities is studied: Cléry's powder against Exibard's powder."},
